From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: premohq <48417750+premohq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:03:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5-ECAM's Switch side: a game's update and DLC beside it,
 wherever its games folder is

Eden took a game's update and DLC from the game files folder's updates/, and from the game's own
folder only when that folder was in roms/. PS5-ECAM's Switch side lists games from any folder (a USB
drive's, one chosen in Settings > Game files), each "alone or in a folder of its own with its update
and DLC", and leaves the update and DLC files it finds there out of the library as the game's: those
games ran without them, at their first version and with no DLC. Update and DLC files beside a game
directly in roms/ were never read either.

- PS5-ECAM says where it lists its games from (--set games_folder): a game in a folder of its own
  there brings that folder's update, DLC, mods, cheats and post-processing, as roms/<folder>/ does.
  Of roms/ and that folder, the one closer to the game decides, so a games folder above roms/ never
  makes all of roms/ one game's folder.
- A game with no folder of its own: the NSP and XCI files beside it that hold its update or DLC, by
  the title ID in their names, else by what they hold (eden_rom_holds_addon). Another game's files
  are neither handed to Eden nor kept open.
- dlc/ in the game files folder is read as updates/ is, as the other systems' folders have one.

headless/game_addons.h has the rules; PS5-ECAM's tools/tests/test-eden-addons.sh checks them.
